id: ride
name: Ride
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 2/round
exploitable: If you are in the Melee Range of an Opponent
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Get into a Vehicle beside you - at its controls if nobody is - or, in one, get out of it, stop Piloting it, or try to take
  its controls.
# The user's text (2026-11-15), word for word.
text: >
  Ride Maneuver [2/Round]: Take control of a vehicle to ride across the battlefield in style.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: If you are in the Melee Range of an Opponent
  –Effect: Enter an adjacent Vehicle or Battle Jacket if you are not already in a Vehicle or Battle Jacket, then you may
  become the Pilot if there is no Pilot. If you are already in a Vehicle or Battle Jacket, upon using this Maneuver, you
  may either:
  • Leave that Vehicle/Battle Jacket to move onto an unoccupied Square adjacent to that Vehicle/Battle Jacket.
  • Stop Piloting this Vehicle/Battle Jacket and move to an unoccupied Square within the Vehicle/Battle Jacket.
  • Attempt to become the Pilot of the Vehicle/Battle Jacket. If the current Pilot is willing, you become the Pilot in
  their place and swap which Squares you are occupying in the Vehicle/Battle Jacket. If not, make a Clash (Physical Strike
  vs Physical Strike/Dodge). If you win, you become the Pilot. The winner of the Clash may choose to remove the other
  Character involved in the Clash from the Vehicle/Battle Jacket, placing them on a Square adjacent to the Vehicle/Battle
  Jacket of their choice.

---

# No script: it moves tokens and writes a Vehicle's Crew, which a script cannot reach - vehicles.mjs askRide (asked before it is
# paid: which Vehicle beside you, and as Pilot or Passenger; in one, Leave / Stop Piloting / become the Pilot) and doRide (done,
# said on its card). A Pilot needs 1+ Pilot Rank, and a Vehicle with Life Points left. The token goes to the first unoccupied
# Square in the Vehicle - the Pilot to the Pilot Seat - or beside it when leaving; none free, the table places it.
# The Pilot asked whether they are willing; not, the Clash (Physical Strike vs Physical Strike/Dodge) on a card of its own,
# settled in chat.mjs (clash.ride), the winner asked whether the other goes out. Battle Jackets are not built yet.
